  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing sector (NAICS 339112) has seen $871M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The sector recorded 9,196 awards and an average award size of $94.7K. Obligations are down 45.9% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows larger past totals, including $2.3B in FY21, $1.1B in FY22, $1.5B in FY23, $2B in FY24, and $1.6B in FY25. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer in the current year, obligated $740M. The Department of Defense obligated $59M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $50.9M in FY2026 to date. SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC is the largest vendor so far, obligated $144M, followed by FIRST NATION GROUP LLC at $97.6M and OLYMPUS AMERICA INC at $80.9M. This mix of high dependence on one agency and a concentrated set of top vendors frames near-term competition and program risk for contractors working in NAICS 339112.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal spending trended for NAICS 339112?",
        "body": "The sector obligated $871M in FY2026 to date, down 45.9% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations peaked at $2.3B in FY21 and have since fluctuated: $1.1B in FY22, $1.5B in FY23, $2B in FY24, and $1.6B in FY25. The current-year total is partial because fiscal year to date figures are incomplete."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who drives demand and which contractors capture the most business?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligated $740M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $59M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $50.9M. SDV OFFICE SYSTEMS LLC, FIRST NATION GROUP LLC, and OLYMPUS AMERICA INC are the top three vendors, obligated $144M, $97.6M, and $80.9M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does the federal government spend on NAICS 339112?",
      "a": "The federal government obligated $871M on NAICS 339112 in FY2026 to date. The sector recorded 9,196 awards and an average award size of $94.7K, and obligations are down 45.9% year over year. Historical fiscal-year obligations were $2.3B in FY21, $1.1B in FY22, $1.5B in FY23, $2B in FY24, and $1.6B in FY25."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy the most NAICS 339112 services?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer of NAICS 339112 services, obligated $740M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $59M and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $50.9M, followed by the Department of Justice at $16.3M and other agencies with smaller totals."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest NAICS 339112 government contractors?",
